# DMThread — a 1:1 conversation: the messages (newest at the bottom, live over
# SSE), the composer, a "mark read" control, and the OTHER participant's
# TypingIndicator. Takes the Thread row — two participants `a` and `b`, and
# each side's read marker `readA` / `readB`, which is what makes unread counts
# and "Seen" receipts a pure predicate over the row instead of a per-user table
# the language would need `let id = add …` to seed. `draft` is the host's
# `@client` text; `send(thread, body)` and `markRead(thread)` the host actions,
# both `requires participant(thread)`.
#
# `asOf` and the `Typing` row it is compared against are exactly
# live/typing.fct's own documented shape (a heartbeat timestamp, not a flag):
# the host owns the clock instant (see live/timeago.fct — a view cannot read
# it) and a `Typing` row per active typer, `{ thread, who, at }`. What is new
# this round is the WRITE side: `input`'s `on change` dispatch fires `typing`
# as the composer's own text changes, debounced to one dispatch per pause
# rather than one per keystroke — the first real trigger for a heartbeat that,
# before now, nothing in the language could invoke from the act of typing
# itself. The host still owns advancing `asOf` (an `after`-driven tick next to
# `use DMThread`, per chatpanelslowmode.fct's own header on why a component
# cannot own its own `after`), and the countdown lives entirely in the
# comparison `asOf - ty.at < 5`, never in a stored flag or a removal job.
import "messagebubble.fct"
import "../live/typing.fct"
app FacetChat:
    component DMThread(t: Thread, draft: cell text, asOf: int):
        box class "x-thread":
            box class "x-thread-list":
                for m in Message where m.thread == t.id by sent desc limit 200:
                    use MessageBubble(m, m.from == actor, (t.a == actor && m.sent <= t.readB) || (t.b == actor && m.sent <= t.readA))
                if t.a == actor:
                    if exists(ty in Typing where ty.thread == t.id && ty.who != actor && asOf - ty.at < 5):
                        use TypingIndicator(t.b)
                if t.b == actor:
                    if exists(ty in Typing where ty.thread == t.id && ty.who != actor && asOf - ty.at < 5):
                        use TypingIndicator(t.a)
            row class "x-composer":
                form "Send" -> send(t.id, draft):
                    input bind draft placeholder "Message" on change -> typing(t.id) debounce 1s
                button "Mark read" -> markRead(t.id) class "x-pill x-small"
